        "type": "Module",
        "name": "usb_to_uart_bridge",
        "description": "CH340 USB-to-UART bridge. Functional purpose: converts USB signals (UD_P, UD_N) to serial UART signals (TXD, RXD). Key interfaces: USB differential pair input, UART TX/RX output, internally generated 3.3V rail (V3) used to power the chip core and possibly external logic. Critical configuration: XI and XO pins require an external crystal (added later) to set oscillator frequency; all unused UART flow control pins (CTS, DSR, RI, DCD, DTR, RTS, R232) should be configured for disabled state via pull-up/down resistors (added later). The module owns its own 3.3V rail (V3), which is generated internally from USB_5V via a regulator network; this rail is exposed for downstream use.",
        "id": "usb_to_uart_bridge"
      },
